==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|spontaneus||voluntary}}. Compare {{cog|fr|spontanéité}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈspɒn.tə.neɪ.ə.ti/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-spontaneity.ogg|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[spontaneous]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tessa Solomon|title=AI Art Lacking ‘Human Expression’ Cannot Be Copyrighted, US Officials Say|magazine=w:ARTnews|url=https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/ai-art-human-expression-copyright-us-report-1234731287/|date=2025-01-30|passage=The unpredictability of Gemini was then contrasted with examples of human '''spontaneity''', like the splatter technique of Jackson Pollock.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} {{U|spontaneous}} [[behaviour]].
#* {{RQ:Browning Aurora Leigh|book=3|text=Romney Leigh, who lives by diagrams, / And crosses out the '''spontaneities''' / Of all his individual, personal life / With formal universals.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} The tendency to [[undergo]] [[change]], characteristic of both animal and vegetable organisms, and not restrained or checked by the [[environment]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} The tendency to activity of [[muscular]] [[tissue]], including the voluntary muscles, when in a state of healthful vigour and refreshment.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being spontaneous}} {{l|en|abruptness}}, {{l|en|spontaneousness}}; see also [[Thesaurus:suddenness]]

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|quality of being spontaneous}} {{l|en|discipline}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|spontaneous}}

